// EXPECT-DIAG: E139
// EXPECT-DIAG: '5.' ends in a '.' with no digit after it
// A bare trailing dot (`5.`, nothing after it) is not a number: FREEZE.md's
// dotted-float grammar requires at least one fractional digit after '.'.
// The lexer used to return `5` and leave the '.' to the parser, which said
// "Expected a method name after '.'" to someone who was writing a decimal
// (issue #263). It is now a malformed number (E139). A letter after the dot
// (`5.name`) is still member access and is NOT rejected here.

fn main(): int {
    mut x: double = 5.;
    return 0;
}
